Smart Shield supersedes Argo Smart Routing; best practices apply. Monitor Cloudflare changelog.

Always check editability before attempting to enable/disable Argo. Set up billing notifications. Combine with Tiered Cache. Use in production only - disable for dev/staging to control costs. Monitor analytics - require 500+ requests in 48h for detailed metrics. Handle errors gracefully - check for billing, permissions, zone compatibility. Test configuration changes in staging before production. Use TypeScript SDK. Implement retry logic. Document zone-specific settings.

Eligibility: Enterprise+ plan, billing/payment configured; contact support if unclear. Require `editable: true`; otherwise check billing, plan, holds/suspensions, and token `Zone:Argo Smart Routing:Edit`.

```ts
const status = await client.argo.smartRouting.get({ zone_id: zoneId });
if (!status.editable) {
console.error("Cannot modify Argo settings:");
throw new Error("Argo is not editable for this zone");
}
await client.argo.smartRouting.edit({ zone_id: zoneId, value: "on" });
```

429 means typically 1200 requests/5 minutes:
```ts
import { RateLimitError } from "cloudflare";
if (error instanceof RateLimitError) {
const retryAfter = error.response?.headers.get("retry-after");
console.log(`Rate limited. Retry after ${retryAfter} seconds`);
await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, (retryAfter || 60) * 1000));
}
```

Analytics: 500/48h, 1–5m latency. Proxied traffic only; DDoS/WAF-mitigated traffic excluded. Spectrum apps: no hard limit.
